{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1771179625925,"sessionID":"ses_39d77dfc2ffeGw9cz50foD28FA","part":{"id":"prt_c62884da9001q0FqvQ9vxTHnul","sessionID":"ses_39d77dfc2ffeGw9cz50foD28FA","messageID":"msg_c6288358a0010yNHpFFtTjQMga","type":"tool","callID":"call_ad39d5d6a0254852a14bef9b","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/specs/grid-interaction.md"},"output":"<path>/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/specs/grid-interaction.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>1: # Spec: Grid Interaction\n2: \n3: ## Overview\n4: Direct manipulation interface for placing and removing cells on the Game of Life grid during PLANNING phase.\n5: \n6: ## Functional Requirements\n7: \n8: ### Placement Mode (PLANNING Phase)\n9: - **Click to Place**: Single click on empty grid cell places a live cell\n10: - **Click to Remove**: Single click on existing live cell removes it and refunds Flux\n11: - **Visual Feedback**: Cursor changes to indicate placeable vs non-placeable areas\n12: - **Minimum Cells Rule**: START button disabled until at least 1 cell has been placed\n13: \n14: ### Interaction Constraints\n15: - Disabled entirely during RUNNING phase\n16: - Disabled during FINISHED phase\n17: - Grid cells must be clickable on both desktop (mouse) and mobile (touch)\n18: - Touch targets minimum 44x44px for mobile accessibility\n19: \n20: ### Coordinate System\n21: ```typescript\n22: interface GridInteraction {\n23:   cellX: number;        // 0 to gridWidth-1\n24:   cellY: number;        // 0 to gridHeight-1\n25:   isPlaceable: boolean; // Calculated based on Flux and existing cell\n26: }\n27: ```\n28: \n29: ## UI/UX Requirements\n30: \n31: ### Cursor States\n32: - **Default**: Standard cursor\n33: - **Over Empty Cell (Placeable)**: Crosshair or cell preview outline\n34: - **Over Empty Cell (Unplaceable)**: Forbidden symbol (Flux = 0)\n35: - **Over Live Cell (Removable)**: Minus icon or highlight\n36: \n37: ### Visual Feedback\n38: - **Cell Preview**: Ghost/outline of cell follows cursor when hovering over grid\n39: - **Cell Placement**: Fade-in animation (0.1s duration)\n40: - **Cell Removal**: Shrink animation (0.15s duration)\n41: - **Invalid Action**: Brief red flash on cursor location\n42: \n43: ### Mobile Considerations\n44: - Pinch-to-zoom disabled on game grid\n45: - Touch-and-hold to drag not needed (single click only)\n46: - Prevent accidental browser zoom on double-tap\n47: - Visual ripple effect on touch\n48: \n49: ## Edge Cases\n50: \n51: 1. **Rapid Clicking**: User might click faster than animation - ensure state consistency\n52: 2. **Edge of Grid**: Clicking exactly on grid boundary should round to nearest cell\n53: 3. **Overlapping with UI**: Ensure grid doesn't extend under HUD elements\n54: 4. **Window Resize**: Grid cells must maintain aspect ratio on resize\n55: \n56: ## Implementation Notes\n57: \n58: - Use event delegation for grid click handling\n59: - Calculate cell coordinates from mouse/touch position: `cellX = Math.floor((x - gridOffsetX) / cellSize)`\n60: - Consider using CSS Grid or Canvas for rendering - Canvas may be better for performance with many cells\n61: - Implement hit testing to distinguish between grid cells and gaps\n62: \n\n(End of file - total 62 lines)\n</content>","title":"specs/grid-interaction.md","metadata":{"preview":"# Spec: Grid Interaction\n\n## Overview\nDirect manipulation interface for placing and removing cells on the Game of Life grid during PLANNING phase.\n\n## Functional Requirements\n\n### Placement Mode (PLANNING Phase)\n- **Click to Place**: Single click on empty grid cell places a live cell\n- **Click to Remove**: Single click on existing live cell removes it and refunds Flux\n- **Visual Feedback**: Cursor changes to indicate placeable vs non-placeable areas\n- **Minimum Cells Rule**: START button disabled until at least 1 cell has been placed\n\n### Interaction Constraints\n- Disabled entirely during RUNNING phase\n- Disabled during FINISHED phase\n- Grid cells must be clickable on both desktop (mouse) and mobile (touch)\n- Touch targets minimum 44x44px for mobile accessibility\n\n### Coordinate System","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"time":{"start":1771179625900,"end":1771179625923}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1771179625928,"sessionID":"ses_39d77dfc2ffeGw9cz50foD28FA","part":{"id":"prt_c62884d99001Ex271YkCccT0nq","sessionID":"ses_39d77dfc2ffeGw9cz50foD28FA","messageID":"msg_c6288358a0010yNHpFFtTjQMga","type":"tool","callID":"call_373b009e25574120b105848d","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/specs/expert-settings.md"},"output":"<path>/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/specs/expert-settings.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>1: # Spec: Expert Settings / Dev Panel\n2: \n3: ## Overview\n4: Hidden configuration interface for tuning game mechanics, balancing parameters, and debugging. Accessible during development and for advanced users to find optimal parametrization.\n5: \n6: ## Functional Requirements\n7: \n8: ### Access Methods\n9: ```typescript\n10: interface ExpertSettingsAccess {\n11:   keyboardShortcut: string;      // '`' (backtick) for quick access\n12:   menuPath: string;              // \"Settings → Advanced → Expert Mode\" (if menu system exists)\n13:   gesture: string;               // Mobile: triple-tap top-left corner\n14: }\n15: ```\n16: \n17: ### Configurable Parameters\n18: \n19: #### Movement Detection Parameters\n20: ```typescript\n21: interface MovementDetectionParams {\n22:   centroidHistoryLength: number;       // Generations to track (default: 5, range: 3-10)\n23:   movementThreshold: number;           // Cells to be \"moving\" (default: 0.5, range: 0.1-2.0)\n24:   minClusterSize: number;            // Minimum cells to track (default: 1, range: 1-5)\n25: }\n26: ```\n27: \n28: #### Scoring Parameters\n29: ```typescript\n30: interface ScoringParams {\n31:   moverPointsPerGeneration: number;      // Default: 10, range: 1-100\n32:   oscillatorPointsPerGeneration: number;   // Default: 2, range: 0-20\n33:   scoreMultiplier: number;                // Default: 1.0, range: 0.1-5.0\n34: }\n35: ```\n36: \n37: #### Level Generation Parameters\n38: ```typescript\n39: interface LevelGenerationParams {\n40:   baseTimeSeconds: number;                // Default: 45, range: 10-120\n41:   timeIncrementPerLevel: number;          // Default: 15, range: 0-60\n42:   baseFlux: number;                       // Default: 20, range: 5-50\n43:   difficultyScalingMode: 'TIME_ONLY' | 'RESOURCE_ONLY' | 'MIXED' | 'EXTREME';\n44: }\n45: ```\n46: \n47: #### Grid Sizing Parameters\n48: ```typescript\n49: interface GridSizingParams {\n50:   mobileCellSize: number;                 // Default: 18, range: 14-24\n51:   desktopCellSize: number;                // Default: 20, range: 16-28\n52:   minVisibleCells: number;                // Default: 10, minimum cells visible\n53: }\n54: ```\n55: \n56: ### Settings Persistence\n57: - Save to localStorage under key `gol-expert-settings`\n58: - Load on app startup\n59: - \"Reset to Defaults\" button with confirmation\n60: - Export/Import settings as JSON (for sharing configurations)\n61: \n62: ## UI/UX Requirements\n63: \n64: ### Panel Layout\n65: - **Position**: Modal overlay, centered or right sidebar\n66: - **Sections**: Collapsible groups by category (Movement, Scoring, Levels, Grid)\n67: - **Controls**:\n68:   - Sliders for numeric ranges\n69:   - Number inputs for precise values\n70:   - Dropdowns for mode selection\n71: \n72: ### Real-Time Updates\n73: - Changes apply immediately (no restart required)\n74: - Visual indicator when value differs from default\n75: - \"Revert\" button per section\n76: - Live preview: Show parameter effects in real-time if possible\n77: \n78: ### Danger Zone\n79: - Separate section for \"Break Things\" settings\n80: - Require confirmation for extreme values\n81: - Show warning if settings would make game impossible\n82: \n83: ### Export/Import\n84: - \"Export JSON\" button downloads current config\n85: - \"Import JSON\" file picker loads config\n86: - Validate imported JSON against schema\n87: \n88: ## Edge Cases\n89: \n90: 1. **Invalid Values**: Input validation prevents negative numbers, out-of-range values\n91: 2. **Settings While Running**: Changes to scoring apply immediately; level changes apply on next level\n92: 3. **Reset During Game**: Reset to defaults should warn if game in progress\n93: 4. **Corrupted Storage**: If localStorage has invalid JSON, fall back to defaults\n94: 5. **Mobile Access**: Ensure gesture detection doesn't conflict with game controls\n95: \n96: ## Implementation Notes\n97: \n98: - Use React Context or Zustand for settings state\n99: - Validate all inputs with constraints\n100: - Schema validation using Zod or similar\n101: - Default values should create balanced, playable game\n102: - Consider \"Presets\" dropdown (\"Easy\", \"Normal\", \"Hard\", \"Chaos\")\n103: - Expert settings should be accessible but not intrusive\n104: - Document each parameter with tooltip explaining its effect\n105: \n\n(End of file - total 105 lines)\n</content>","title":"specs/expert-settings.md","metadata":{"preview":"# Spec: Expert Settings / Dev Panel\n\n## Overview\nHidden configuration interface for tuning game mechanics, balancing parameters, and debugging. Accessible during development and for advanced users to find optimal parametrization.\n\n## Functional Requirements\n\n### Access Methods\n```typescript\ninterface ExpertSettingsAccess {\n  keyboardShortcut: string;      // '`' (backtick) for quick access\n  menuPath: string;              // \"Settings → Advanced → Expert Mode\" (if menu system exists)\n  gesture: string;               // Mobile: triple-tap top-left corner\n}\n```\n\n### Configurable Parameters\n\n#### Movement Detection Parameters\n```typescript","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"time":{"start":1771179625883,"end":1771179625926}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1771179625930,"sessionID":"ses_39d77dfc2ffeGw9cz50foD28FA","part":{"id":"prt_c62884d9d001Exo0vzfZEBTi2a","sessionID":"ses_39d77dfc2ffeGw9cz50foD28FA","messageID":"msg_c6288358a0010yNHpFFtTjQMga","type":"tool","callID":"call_548e111f4020480084186dd3","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/specs/level-progression.md"},"output":"<path>/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/specs/level-progression.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>1: # Spec: Level Progression\n2: \n3: ## Overview\n4: Progressive difficulty system where players advance through levels with increasing time limits and limited Flux. The goal is to maximize points within each level's time limit and Flux budget.\n5: \n6: ## Functional Requirements\n7: \n8: ### Level Configuration Schema\n9: ```typescript\n10: interface LevelConfig {\n11:   levelNumber: number;\n12:   timeLimitSeconds: number;    // Increases with each level\n13:   initialFlux: number;          // Flux available for the level\n14: }\n15: \n16: interface LevelProgression {\n17:   currentLevel: number;\n18:   maxUnlockedLevel: number;      // For future: level select screen\n19:   totalScore: number;            // Cumulative score across all levels\n20:   levels: LevelConfig[];         // Array of level definitions\n21: }\n22: ```\n23: \n24: ### Difficulty Scaling (Expert Settings Configurable)\n25: Default strategy: **Increase time for difficulty**\n26: \n27: ```typescript\n28: const defaultLevelGeneration = (levelNum: number): LevelConfig => ({\n29:   levelNumber: levelNum,\n30:   timeLimitSeconds: 45 + (levelNum - 1) * 15,  // 45, 60, 75, 90...\n31:   initialFlux: 20                            // Constant for now\n32: });\n33: ```\n34: \n35: Alternative strategies (selectable in Expert Settings):\n36: - **Time Only**: Increase time, constant Flux\n37: - **Resource Only**: Constant time, decrease Flux\n38: - **Mixed**: Both time and Flux adjusted\n39: - **Extreme**: Increase time slightly but aggressively reduce Flux\n40: \n41: ### Progression Flow\n42: 1. Player completes level N (timer reaches 0 or all cells die)\n43: 2. Screen fades out over 2.0s\n44: 3. Loading/interstitial (2.0s)\n45: 4. Screen fades in to level N+1 with fresh grid\n46: 5. Reset to PLANNING phase with fresh Flux\n47: 6. Score accumulated across all levels\n48: \n49: ### Game Objective\n50: - **Goal**: Maximize points within time limit and Flux budget\n51: - **Score Calculation**: Based on kinetic energy, cell activity, and survival (see scoring-system.md)\n52: - **Level Completion**: Timer reaches 0 OR all cells die (score stops accumulating)\n53: - **No Lose Condition**: Game always advances to next level; only score accumulation varies\n54: \n55: ## UI/UX Requirements\n56: \n57: ### Level Display\n58: - **Current Level**: Show \"Level X\" in corner of screen\n59: - **Progress**: Optional progress bar showing X of Y levels\n60: - **Level Complete**: Brief \"Level X Complete\" message during transition\n61: \n62: ### Transition Effects\n63: - **Fade Out**: 2.0s ease-out to black\n64: - **Interstitial**: Level number display (2.0s)\n65: - **Fade In**: 2.0s ease-in from black\n66: - **Sound**: Transition whoosh/complete sound effect\n67: - **Skip**: Press Space/ESC to skip to next level immediately\n68: \n69: ### End of Game\n70: - After final level (configurable, default 10), show victory screen\n71: - Display total accumulated score across all levels\n72: - Option to restart from level 1 or return to menu\n73: \n74: ## Edge Cases\n75: \n76: 1. **Level 0 or Invalid**: Default to level 1 if undefined\n77: 2. **Last Level**: Show victory screen with total score\n78: 3. **Browser Refresh**: Save progress in localStorage? (Optional persistence)\n79: 4. **All Cells Die Early**: Level ends immediately, score stops accumulating, game advances to next level\n80: \n81: ## Implementation Notes\n82: \n83: - Store level configs in JSON or TypeScript object\n84: - Generate levels dynamically or use static array\n85: - Total levels configurable in Expert Settings\n86: - Level progression increments on level completion (no win/lose condition)\n87: - Score accumulates across all levels (totalScore tracked separately)\n88: - Fade transitions use CSS opacity with 2s duration\n89: - Simulation stops when level ends, starts fresh for next level (no carryover)\n90: \n\n(End of file - total 90 lines)\n</content>","title":"specs/level-progression.md","metadata":{"preview":"# Spec: Level Progression\n\n## Overview\nProgressive difficulty system where players advance through levels with increasing time limits and limited Flux. The goal is to maximize points within each level's time limit and Flux budget.\n\n## Functional Requirements\n\n### Level Configuration Schema\n```typescript\ninterface LevelConfig {\n  levelNumber: number;\n  timeLimitSeconds: number;    // Increases with each level\n  initialFlux: number;          // Flux available for the level\n}\n\ninterface LevelProgression {\n  currentLevel: number;\n  maxUnlockedLevel: number;      // For future: level select screen\n  totalScore: number;            // Cumulative score across all levels\n  levels: LevelConfig[];         // Array of level definitions","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"time":{"start":1771179625888,"end":1771179625928}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1771179625932,"sessionID":"ses_39d77dfc2ffeGw9cz50foD28FA","part":{"id":"prt_c62884d93001Cwu61zFR78Lg2T","sessionID":"ses_39d77dfc2ffeGw9cz50foD28FA","messageID":"msg_c6288358a0010yNHpFFtTjQMga","type":"tool","callID":"call_99e981bc98674af687038ccd","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/specs/auto-advance-transitions.md"},"output":"<path>/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/specs/auto-advance-transitions.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>1: # Spec: Auto-Advance Transitions\n2: \n3: ## Overview\n4: Seamless level progression system with cinematic fade transitions between completed levels.\n5: \n6: ## Functional Requirements\n7: \n8: ### Transition Trigger\n9: ```typescript\n10: interface TransitionConfig {\n11:   fadeOutDuration: number;        // Default: 2.0s\n12:   fadeInDuration: number;         // Default: 2.0s\n13:   interstitialDuration: number;   // Default: 2.0s (black screen)\n14:   autoAdvanceDelay: number;       // Default: 2.0s (time on finished screen)\n15:   skipEnabled: boolean;            // Allow skipping transitions (Space/ESC)\n16: }\n17: ```\n18: \n19: ```typescript\n20: type TransitionState = \n21:   | 'PLAYING'           // Normal gameplay\n22:   | 'FADING_OUT'        // Fade to black\n23:   | 'INTERSTITIAL'      // Black screen, show level info\n24:   | 'FADING_IN'         // Fade from black\n25:   | 'READY';            // Next level loaded, waiting for input\n26: ```\n27: \n28: ### Transition Sequence\n29: \n30: #### FINISHED → Next Level (Success)\n31: 1. **FINISHED Phase Display** (2.0s):\n32:    - Show final score\n33:    - Show \"Level Complete\" text\n34:    - Continue rendering simulation (visual only, no scoring)\n35:    - **SKIP**: Press Space/ESC to skip to fade out immediately\n36: \n37: 2. **Fade Out** (2.0s):\n38:    - Full-screen black overlay opacity 0→1\n39:    - Easing: ease-in-out\n40:    - Simulation continues but hidden\n41:    - **SKIP**: Press Space/ESC to skip to interstitial immediately\n42: \n43: 3. **Interstitial** (2.0s):\n44:    - Full black screen\n45:    - Center: \"Level X Complete\" (fading out)\n46:    - Center: \"Level X+1\" (fading in)\n47:    - Load next level configuration\n48:    - Reset game state (Flux, Score resets - no carryover between levels)\n49:    - **SKIP**: Press Space/ESC to skip to fade in immediately\n50: \n51: 4. **Fade In** (2.0s):\n52:    - Black overlay opacity 1→0\n53:    - New level visible with fresh grid\n54:    - Simulation stopped, waiting for countdown to finish\n55:    - PLANNING phase ready after countdown\n56:    - **SKIP**: Press Space/ESC to skip to READY immediately\n57: \n58: 5. **READY**:\n59:    - Player can immediately start placing cells\n60: \n61: #### FINISHED → Game Over (Failure)\n62: - Similar fade sequence but to \"Game Over\" screen\n63: - Option to \"Retry Level\" or \"Return to Menu\"\n64: - No auto-advance on failure (wait for input)\n65: \n66: ## UI/UX Requirements\n67: \n68: ### Fade Overlay\n69: - **Element**: Fixed position div covering viewport\n70: - **Color**: Black (#000000)\n71: - **Z-Index**: Above all game elements, below modals\n72: - **Pointer Events**: None (let clicks pass through if needed)\n73: \n74: ### Interstitial Display\n75: - **Level Complete Text**: \"Level X Complete\" - fade out during fade-to-black\n76: - **Next Level Text**: \"Level X+1\" - fade in during fade-from-black\n77: - **Font**: Large, bold, centered\n78: - **Optional**: Show quick stats (\"Score: Y\")\n79: \n80: ### Skip Indicator\n81: - **Prompt**: \"Press Space or ESC to skip\" (small text at bottom)\n82: - **Visibility**: Shown during all transition phases\n83: - **Fade out**: Hide during READY state\n84: \n85: ### Audio\n86: - **Fade Out**: \"Level Complete\" chime/sound\n87: - **Interstitial**: Brief ambient or silence\n88: - **Fade In**: \"Level Start\" sound (distinct from first level)\n89: \n90: ### Visual Effects\n91: - **Blur**: Slight blur on game during fade (optional polish)\n92: - **Progress**: Optional progress bar showing \"X of Y levels\"\n93: \n94: ## Edge Cases\n95: \n96:  1. **Browser Tab During Transition**: If user switches tabs mid-transition:\n97:      - Pause transition timer to prevent level from advancing unseen\n98:      - Resume when tab becomes active again\n99:      - Note: This only applies to transitions - during gameplay, the game timer continues running when tab is inactive\n100: \n101:  2. **Rapid Success**: Player beating levels very quickly:\n102:      - Skip mechanism prevents transitions from feeling tedious\n103:      - Allow holding Space/ESC to skip all transitions\n104: \n105:  3. **Last Level**: After final level:\n106:      - Fade to \"Victory\" screen instead of next level\n107:      - Show total score accumulated across all levels\n108:      - Provide \"Play Again\" or \"Return to Level 1\"\n109: \n110:  4. **Interruption**: Player presses key during transition:\n111:      - Space/Escape: Skip to end of transition (immediately jump to READY state)\n112:      - Skip works at any point during transition sequence\n113: \n114:  5. **Performance**: Low-end devices might struggle with opacity animations:\n115:      - Use CSS `will-change: opacity`\n116:      - Consider reducing animation complexity\n117: \n118: ## Implementation Notes\n119: \n120: - Use CSS transitions for smooth 60fps fades\n121: - React state machine for transition phases\n122: - Preload next level assets during fade-out if possible\n123: - Audio: Fade volume during transition (not abrupt cut)\n124: - Mobile: Ensure transitions work with reduced motion preferences (accessibility)\n125: - Skip transitions configurable in Expert Settings\n126: - Test with all browser zoom levels to ensure overlay covers fully\n127: \n\n(End of file - total 127 lines)\n</content>","title":"specs/auto-advance-transitions.md","metadata":{"preview":"# Spec: Auto-Advance Transitions\n\n## Overview\nSeamless level progression system with cinematic fade transitions between completed levels.\n\n## Functional Requirements\n\n### Transition Trigger\n```typescript\ninterface TransitionConfig {\n  fadeOutDuration: number;        // Default: 2.0s\n  fadeInDuration: number;         // Default: 2.0s\n  interstitialDuration: number;   // Default: 2.0s (black screen)\n  autoAdvanceDelay: number;       // Default: 2.0s (time on finished screen)\n  skipEnabled: boolean;            // Allow skipping transitions (Space/ESC)\n}\n```\n\n```typescript\ntype TransitionState = ","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"time":{"start":1771179625879,"end":1771179625930}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1771179625934,"sessionID":"ses_39d77dfc2ffeGw9cz50foD28FA","part":{"id":"prt_c62884da40012FAgPi0tHyWLQv","sessionID":"ses_39d77dfc2ffeGw9cz50foD28FA","messageID":"msg_c6288358a0010yNHpFFtTjQMga","type":"tool","callID":"call_9d024a4b1f4e4703b43e7b40","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/specs/user-interaction.md"},"output":"<path>/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/specs/user-interaction.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>1: # Spec: User Interaction System\n2: \n3: ## Overview\n4: The user interaction system handles mouse and touch input for drawing and erasing cells on the grid with real-time visual feedback and sound generation.\n5: \n6: ## Functional Requirements\n7: \n8: ### Interaction Modes\n9: ```typescript\n10: type InteractionMode = 'draw' | 'erase';\n11: ```\n12: \n13: **Draw Mode**: Click/drag to place live cells (age=1)\n14: **Erase Mode**: Click/drag to remove cells (set to 0)\n15: \n16: ### Mouse Interaction\n17: \n18: #### Mouse Down\n19: 1. Capture mouse position relative to canvas\n20: 2. Convert to grid coordinates: `c = floor(x / (canvasWidth / numCols))`\n21: 3. Trigger interaction handler with type='down'\n22: \n23: #### Mouse Move (while pressed)\n24: 1. Capture mouse position\n25: 2. Convert to grid coordinates\n26: 3. Trigger interaction handler with type='enter'\n27: \n28: #### Mouse Up (global)\n29: 1. Set `isMouseDown` state to false\n30: 2. Prevent stale drag state\n31: \n32: ### Touch Interaction\n33: \n34: #### Touch Start\n35: 1. Prevent default (stop scrolling)\n36: 2. Capture first touch position\n37: 3. Convert to grid coordinates\n38: 4. Trigger interaction handler with type='down'\n39: \n40: #### Touch Move\n41: 1. Prevent default (stop scrolling)\n42: 2. Capture first touch position\n43: 3. Convert to grid coordinates\n44: 4. Trigger interaction handler with type='enter'\n45: \n46: #### Touch End / Cancel\n47: 1. Set `isMouseDown` state to false\n48: \n49: ## Implementation Architecture\n50: \n51: ### Coordinate Mapping\n52: ```typescript\n53: interface GridCoordinates {\n54:   row: number; // 0 to numRows-1\n55:   col: number; // 0 to numCols-1\n56: }\n57: \n58: function getCellFromEvent(\n59:   event: MouseEvent | TouchEvent,\n60:   canvas: HTMLCanvasElement,\n61:   numRows: number,\n62:   numCols: number\n63: ): GridCoordinates\n64: ```\n65: \n66: ### Interaction Handler\n67: ```typescript\n68: function handleCellInteract(\n69:   row: number,\n70:   col: number,\n71:   type: 'down' | 'enter'\n72: ): void\n73: ```\n74: \n75: - **type='down'**: Modify cell(s)\n76: - **type='enter'**: Only modify if mouse down\n77: \n78: ### Sound Integration\n79: - **Draw/Erase**: Play interaction sound (different tones)\n80: - **Sound Engine**: Called per cell interaction\n81: \n82: ## Edge Cases\n83: \n84: 1. **Boundary Coordinates**: Math.floor() ensures valid indices\n85: 2. **Rapid Clicking**: Multiple clicks allowed\n86: 3. **Canvas Resize**: Grid dimensions update, coordinates recalculate\n87: 4. **Touch Conflicts**: PreventDefault() blocks browser zoom/scroll\n88: 5. **Mouse Leave Canvas**: Set isMouseDown to false to stop drag\n89: \n90: ## Mobile Considerations\n91: \n92: - **Touch Action**: `touch-action: none` on canvas element\n93: - **Target Size**: Responsive cell size (18px mobile, 20px desktop) meets minimum touch target\n94: - **Prevent Default**: Stop scrolling while drawing\n95: - **Multi-touch**: Only first touch used (ignore additional touches)\n96: \n97: ## Visual Feedback\n98: \n99: - **Cursor**: `crosshair` style over canvas\n100: - **Hover Effects**: None (draw directly on grid)\n101: - **Selection Feedback**: No preview shown (immediate drawing)\n102: \n103: ## Dependencies\n104: \n105: - Core simulation engine: Grid ref and dimensions\n106: - Audio sonification system: Play interaction sounds\n107: - Canvas rendering system: Redraw on state change\n108: \n\n(End of file - total 108 lines)\n</content>","title":"specs/user-interaction.md","metadata":{"preview":"# Spec: User Interaction System\n\n## Overview\nThe user interaction system handles mouse and touch input for drawing and erasing cells on the grid with real-time visual feedback and sound generation.\n\n## Functional Requirements\n\n### Interaction Modes\n```typescript\ntype InteractionMode = 'draw' | 'erase';\n```\n\n**Draw Mode**: Click/drag to place live cells (age=1)\n**Erase Mode**: Click/drag to remove cells (set to 0)\n\n### Mouse Interaction\n\n#### Mouse Down\n1. Capture mouse position relative to canvas\n2. Convert to grid coordinates: `c = floor(x / (canvasWidth / numCols))`","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"time":{"start":1771179625894,"end":1771179625933}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1771179625937,"sessionID":"ses_39d77dfc2ffeGw9cz50foD28FA","part":{"id":"prt_c62884daf001YjB0vzAmSenSKJ","sessionID":"ses_39d77dfc2ffeGw9cz50foD28FA","messageID":"msg_c6288358a0010yNHpFFtTjQMga","type":"tool","callID":"call_52089f9433494e7391659865","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/specs/ui-overlay.md"},"output":"<path>/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/specs/ui-overlay.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>1: # Spec: UI/Overlay System\n2: \n3: ## Overview\n4: The UI system provides controls, configuration panels, and visual overlays including a cinematic intro, HUD controls, and responsive interface management for the Game of Life application.\n5: \n6: ## Functional Requirements\n7: \n8: ### Cinematic Intro Overlay\n9: \n10: **Behavior**:\n11: - Shows on app load\n12: - Displays title: \"CONWAY'S GAME OF LIFE\" with glitch effect\n13: - CTA button: \"ENTER VOID\"\n14: - Exit animation: 1.2s fade/scale transition\n15: \n16: **State**:\n17: ```typescript\n18: interface IntroState {\n19:   isIntro: boolean;    // Showing intro\n20:   isExiting: boolean;  // Playing exit animation\n21: }\n22: ```\n23: \n24: **UI State During Intro**:\n25: - Game renders in background\n26: - UI controls hidden\n27: - Audio may play (attract mode)\n28: \n29: ### Main Controls (HUD)\n30: \n31: **Glass HUD Container**:\n32: - Semi-transparent glass effect\n33: - Floating overlay on bottom of screen\n34: - Groups: Main controls, interaction modes, status\n35: \n36: **Main Control Buttons**:\n37: - **PLAY/PAUSE**: Toggle simulation running state\n38: - **STEP**: Execute single generation (disabled while running)\n39: - **RANDOM**: Fill grid randomly (15% cell density)\n40: - **CLEAR**: Remove all cells, reset generation (red text color)\n41: \n42: **Interaction Mode Buttons**:\n43: - **DRAW**: Enable cell placement mode (active state highlighted)\n44: - **ERASE**: Enable cell removal mode (active state highlighted)\n45: \n46: **Status Controls**:\n47: - **Waveform Selector**: Dropdown (Sine, Triangle, Square, Saw)\n48: - **Volume Slider**: Range 0-0.5, 0.01 step\n49: - **Generation Counter**: Display \"GEN: {number}\"\n50: - **Settings Toggle**: Gear icon button (⚙️)\n51: \n52: ### Phase Status Display\n53: \n54: **Visibility**: Always visible\n55: \n56: **Layout**:\n57: - Shows current phase: PLANNING, COUNTDOWN, RUNNING, FINISHED\n58: - Timer display (visible during COUNTDOWN and RUNNING phases)\n59: - Flux counter (visible during PLANNING and RUNNING phases)\n60: \n61: ### Settings Panel\n62: \n63: **Access**: Click gear icon in HUD\n64: \n65: **Configuration Options**:\n66: \n67: 1. **Speed**: Slider (10ms to 500ms)\n68: \n69: 2. **Grid Size**: Buttons for Small (20×30), Medium (40×50), Large (60×80)\n70: \n71: 3. **Visuals**:\n72:    - Checkbox: Show grid lines\n73: \n74: 4. **Audio**:\n75:    - Checkbox: Enable sonification\n76: \n77: 5. **Expert Settings**:\n78:    - Access to Expert Settings panel (for tuning game parameters)\n79: \n80: **Close**: × button in header\n81: \n82: ### UI Toggle\n83: \n84: **Toggle Button**:\n85: - Icon frame (minimal)\n86: - Click to show/hide all UI\n87: - Hidden when `enableUI` prop is false (intro mode)\n88: - Position: Fixed corner\n89: \n90: ## Implementation Architecture\n91: \n92: ### State Management\n93: \n94: ```typescript\n95: interface UIState {\n96:   isUiVisible: boolean;        // Master visibility toggle\n97:   isIntro: boolean;            // Intro overlay active\n98:   isExiting: boolean;          // Intro exit animation\n99:   showSettings: boolean;       // Settings panel open\n100:   enableUI: boolean;           // Prop from App (false during intro)\n101: }\n102: ```\n103: \n104: ### Component Hierarchy\n105: \n106: ```\n107: App\n108: ├── IntroOverlay (conditional on isIntro)\n109: ├── GameOfLife\n110: │   ├── CanvasGrid\n111: │   ├── UIToggleButton\n112: │   └── GlassHUDContainer (conditional on enableUI && isUiVisible)\n113: │       ├── GlassHUD\n114: │       └── SettingsPanel (conditional on showSettings)\n115: ```\n116: \n117: ## CSS Architecture\n118: \n119: ### Glass Effect\n120: ```css\n121: .glass-hud {\n122:   background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);\n123:   backdrop-filter: blur(10px);\n124:   border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.2);\n125:   border-radius: 12px;\n126: }\n127: ```\n128: \n129: ### Button States\n130: - **Active**: Highlighted background/border\n131: - **Disabled**: Opacity reduced, no pointer events\n132: - **Hover**: Slight brightness increase\n133: \n134: ### Animations\n135: - **Intro Exit**: Scale and fade out over 1.2s\n136: - **Panel Open**: Slide in from side\n137: - **Button Hover**: Scale/brightness transition\n138: \n139: ## Responsive Design\n140: \n141: - **Desktop**: Full width HUD centered at bottom\n142: - **Mobile**: Controls may stack or scroll\n143: - **Touch**: Minimum 44px touch targets\n144: - **Canvas**: Adapts to window size, grid scales accordingly\n145: \n146: ## Edge Cases\n147: \n148: 1. **Intro Exit**: Wait 1.2s for animation before removing component\n149: 2. **UI Hidden**: All controls invisible, toggle button still accessible\n150: 3. **Settings During Run**: Settings apply immediately, no pause required\n151: 4. **Grid Size Change**: Resets simulation\n152: 5. **Clear Grid**: Removes all cells, resets generation\n153: \n154: ## Dependencies\n155: \n156: - All systems: Configurable via settings panel\n157: - Core simulation: Speed and size settings affect simulation\n158: - Audio system: Enable toggle controls sonification\n159: - Canvas rendering: Grid line option\n160: - User interaction: Mode buttons select draw/erase\n161: - Phase management: Phase display shows current game state\n162: \n\n(End of file - total 162 lines)\n</content>","title":"specs/ui-overlay.md","metadata":{"preview":"# Spec: UI/Overlay System\n\n## Overview\nThe UI system provides controls, configuration panels, and visual overlays including a cinematic intro, HUD controls, and responsive interface management for the Game of Life application.\n\n## Functional Requirements\n\n### Cinematic Intro Overlay\n\n**Behavior**:\n- Shows on app load\n- Displays title: \"CONWAY'S GAME OF LIFE\" with glitch effect\n- CTA button: \"ENTER VOID\"\n- Exit animation: 1.2s fade/scale transition\n\n**State**:\n```typescript\ninterface IntroState {\n  isIntro: boolean;    // Showing intro\n  isExiting: boolean;  // Playing exit animation","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"time":{"start":1771179625905,"end":1771179625935}}}}
