{"type":"text","timestamp":1771179818719,"sessionID":"ses_39d77dfc2ffeGw9cz50foD28FA","part":{"id":"prt_c628b3ebf001ghr3FbzRQBuaHM","sessionID":"ses_39d77dfc2ffeGw9cz50foD28FA","messageID":"msg_c628ae367001Wz0zeg0oG7humH","type":"text","text":"Now I'll use a general subagent to reason through the best approach and update IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md based on my findings.","time":{"start":1771179818713,"end":1771179818713}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1771179884356,"sessionID":"ses_39d77dfc2ffeGw9cz50foD28FA","part":{"id":"prt_c628b3ec7001H9NSoTGcrz4th0","sessionID":"ses_39d77dfc2ffeGw9cz50foD28FA","messageID":"msg_c628ae367001Wz0zeg0oG7humH","type":"tool","callID":"call_0b431de6b57a4760858317d8","tool":"task","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"description":"Analyze and plan next priorities","prompt":"Based on the comprehensive exploration results, analyze the current state and determine the most important items to address next. Consider:\n\n1. What's already implemented (sprint 1 complete, sprint 2 partial)\n2. Critical gaps (scoring/movement not integrated, no level progression)\n3. Dependencies between features\n4. User experience impact\n\nThen provide:\n1. A prioritized list of top 3-5 items to implement next with justification\n2. For each item, explain what needs to be done\n3. What tests should be added/verified\n4. Any risks or considerations\n\nBe thorough and think about the best path forward to reach a playable game with scoring and level progression.","subagent_type":"general"},"output":"task_id: ses_39d74c132ffe6Zgg8xAb5HYGQ0 (for resuming to continue this task if needed)\n\n<task_result>\nBased on my comprehensive analysis of the codebase, here's the current state and prioritized next steps:\n\n## Current State Summary\n\n**Sprint 1 (COMPLETE)**: Foundation including project setup, types, simulation engine, phase management, canvas rendering, user interaction, flux management, and basic Game component integration. The game is playable - you can place cells and run the simulation.\n\n**Sprint 2 (PARTIAL)**: Movement detection and scoring libraries are fully implemented and tested, ScoreDisplay/GlassHUD/IntroOverlay components exist, BUT **scoring and movement are NOT integrated into the game loop**. The Game component still uses the old manual UI.\n\n**Critical Gaps:**\n1. Movement tracking not running during simulation\n2. Scoring not calculating during generations\n3. Score not displayed in UI\n4. No level progression system\n5. Timer hardcoded to 45s (should scale by level)\n\n---\n\n## Top 5 Prioritized Items\n\n### 1. Integrate Movement Detection & Scoring into Game Loop\n**Why HIGHEST:** Core game mechanics are implemented but not wired together. Without this, the game has no scoring feedback and movement patterns aren't being detected.\n\n**What needs to be done:**\n- In Game component: Add state for `trackedClusters` and `scoreState`\n- In simulation step: Call `findConnectedComponents`, then `trackClusters` to maintain cluster history\n- Call `calculateGenerationScore` each generation and update `scoreState`\n- Use `useRef` for previous tracked clusters (to avoid re-render issues)\n- Integrate ScoreDisplay component into Game UI\n\n**Tests to add/verify:**\n- Test that clusters are tracked across generations\n- Test that scores update correctly based on cluster classifications\n- Test that score resets on level completion\n\n**Risks/Considerations:**\n- Performance: Cluster detection needs to run efficiently (<16ms for 60fps)\n- Circular reference: trackedClusters depends on previous state, careful with useEffect deps\n- Score animation: Need to coordinate with ScoreDisplay's smooth animation\n\n---\n\n### 2. Implement Level Progression System\n**Why HIGH:** No concept of levels, so game has no progression or difficulty scaling. Players can't advance or see level number.\n\n**What needs to be done:**\n- Create `src/lib/level.ts` with `generateLevelConfig` and `createInitialLevelProgression`\n- Implement `LevelProgression` state: `currentLevel`, `totalScore`, `levels[]`\n- Create level generation with difficulty scaling (default: time = 45 + (level-1)*15, flux = 20)\n- Add level display UI in Game component (show \"Level X\")\n- Store total accumulated score across levels\n\n**Tests to add/verify:**\n- Test level config generation for different levels\n- Test difficulty scaling formulas\n- Test level state transitions\n- Test totalScore accumulation across levels\n\n**Risks/Considerations:**\n- Score reset vs total score: Need to clarify per-level score vs cumulative score\n- Level cap: Should be configurable (default 10)\n- Browser refresh: Consider localStorage persistence for progress\n\n---\n\n### 3. Update Phase Timer to Use Level-Specific Duration\n**Why HIGH:** Currently hardcoded to 45s, should scale with level progression (45s, 60s, 75s, etc.)\n\n**What needs to be done:**\n- Modify `usePhaseTimer` hook to accept `levelConfig` as parameter\n- Update `startRunning` call in Game component to use level's `timeLimitSeconds`\n- Ensure timer resets properly on level transitions\n\n**Tests to add/verify:**\n- Test timer uses correct duration for each level\n- Test timer resets on level completion\n- Test countdown still works with variable durations\n\n**Risks/Considerations:**\n- Need to pass level config from Game to usePhaseTimer\n- Ensure phase transitions still work with dynamic timer values\n\n---\n\n### 4. Replace Game Manual UI with GlassHUD Component\n**Why MEDIUM-HIGH:** GlassHUD is complete but Game component still uses inline styles. Better UI architecture and consistency.\n\n**What needs to be done:**\n- Remove manual UI buttons/styling from Game component\n- Import and use GlassHUD component\n- Pass all required props (phase, flux, interactionMode, callbacks, etc.)\n- Add settings panel placeholder (onToggleSettings callback)\n\n**Tests to add/verify:**\n- Test all GlassHUD controls work correctly\n- Test phase/state changes propagate to GlassHUD\n- Test all callbacks fire correctly\n\n**Risks/Considerations:**\n- GlassHUD expects certain props that Game needs to provide\n- Settings panel doesn't exist yet - need stub/mock\n- May need to adjust Game's state management to match GlassHUD expectations\n\n---\n\n### 5. Implement Level Transition Logic\n**Why MEDIUM:** After levels are implemented, need smooth transitions between them (fade out, interstitial, fade in).\n\n**What needs to be done:**\n- Create `src/lib/transitions.ts` with transition state machine\n- Implement `TransitionState`: PLAYING, FADING_OUT, INTERSTITIAL, FADING_IN, READY\n- Add transition animation overlay in Game component\n- Trigger transitions when phase finishes and level advances\n- Reset grid, flux, score on level transition\n\n**Tests to add/verify:**\n- Test transition state machine flow\n- Test transition triggers on level completion\n- Test state resets during transitions\n- Test skip functionality (Space/ESC)\n\n**Risks/Considerations:**\n- Coordinate with phase management (FINISHED → transition → next level PLANNING)\n- Browser tab handling during transitions\n- Transition audio (not yet implemented, will be Sprint 4)\n\n---\n\n## Dependencies Between Items\n\n```\n1. Movement+Scoring Integration\n   ├─ Enables: Score display, pattern breakdown UI\n   └─ Blocks: Meaningful level progression (no score to accumulate)\n   \n2. Level Progression\n   ├─ Enables: Level display, difficulty scaling\n   └─ Blocks: Level transitions, victory screen\n   \n3. Phase Timer Update\n   ├─ Enables: Variable timer per level\n   └─ Blocks: Actual difficulty progression\n   \n4. GlassHUD Integration\n   ├─ Enables: Better UI architecture\n   └─ Blocks: None (can work in parallel)\n   \n5. Level Transitions\n   ├─ Enables: Seamless level progression\n   └─ Blocks: Victory screen\n```\n\n**Recommended implementation order:** 1 → 2 → 3 → 4 → 5 (or 4 in parallel with 2-3)\n\n---\n\n## User Experience Impact\n\n**Current state:** Playable simulation but no scoring feedback, no level progression, static 45s timer.\n\n**After items 1-3:** Complete game loop with scoring, level progression, and difficulty scaling - genuinely playable game.\n\n**After items 4-5:** Polished UI and smooth level transitions - production-ready experience.\n\nItems 1-3 are **critical** for a playable game. Items 4-5 are **important** for polish and UX.\n</task_result>","title":"Analyze and plan next priorities","metadata":{"sessionId":"ses_39d74c132ffe6Zgg8xAb5HYGQ0","model":{"modelID":"glm-4.7","providerID":"zai-coding-plan"},"truncated":false},"time":{"start":1771179818699,"end":1771179884354}}}}
